# The subset of data/ that the running app needs is tracked on purpose:
#   data/corpus       the retrieval corpus (JSON)
#   data/chroma_db    the prebuilt vector index
#   data/models       the ONNX encoder
#   data/regulatory   the source RBI PDFs
#   data/policies     the policies the benchmark was built from
#   data/benchmarks   the labelled benchmark and the written evaluation results
#
# Earlier commits untracked data/ entirely, so the deployed service had no corpus
# and no index: every request answered 200 while every finding cited a hardcoded
# fallback passage. Keep the subset above tracked. What stays ignored is the parts
# that are regenerated or machine-specific: the SQLite audit trail and the pickled
# model. Note that `git add -A` after a clean clone would re-add everything, so add
# files by name.


